dtnmos itself holds no code of others: its JSON, SHA-1 and DNS are its own. A build with
-DDTNMOS_WITH_CURL=ON or -DDTNMOS_WITH_SERVER=ON links the libraries below, and so does a
program that takes the features curl or server of the vcpkg port. Which ones, by the
platform, as vcpkg builds them:

    libcurl    with DTNMOS_WITH_CURL, for HTTP, HTTPS and WebSockets     all platforms
    zlib       with libcurl                                               all platforms
    OpenSSL    with libcurl, for HTTPS; Windows uses its own Schannel     Linux, macOS
    civetweb   with DTNMOS_WITH_SERVER, for the server of a node         all platforms

A program that ships such a build ships these notices with it. The versions the preset
linux-full was last built with are curl 8.21.0, zlib 1.3.2, OpenSSL 3.6.3 and
civetweb 1.16.

